name: high-end-visual-design
description: Teaches the AI to design like a high-end agency. Defines the exact fonts, spacing, shadows, card structures, and animations that make a website feel expensive. Blocks all the common defaults that make AI designs look cheap or generic.

# High-End Visual Design Skill

## Overview
A premium UI/UX architecture skill that produces $150k+ agency-level digital experiences. Enforces haptic depth, cinematic spatial rhythm, obsessive micro-interactions, and flawless fluid motion.

## Key Features
- **Creative Variance Engine**: Combines vibe/texture archetypes with layout archetypes for unique outputs
- **Double-Bezel Architecture**: Nested enclosures for premium card/container design
- **Button-in-Button Pattern**: Premium CTA buttons with nested icon wrappers
- **Fluid Island Nav**: Floating glass pill navigation with staggered mask reveals
- **Magnetic Button Physics**: Spring-based hover interactions
- **Scroll Interpolation**: Heavy fade-up entry animations

## Banned Elements (Absolute Zero)
- Fonts: Inter, Roboto, Arial, Open Sans, Helvetica
- Icons: Lucide, FontAwesome, Material Icons (standard weights)
- Generic 1px gray borders and harsh shadows
- Standard `linear` or `ease-in-out` transitions

## Performance Guardrails
- GPU-safe animations (transform + opacity only)
- backdrop-blur on fixed/sticky elements only
- z-index discipline for systemic layers

## When to Use
- Premium brand websites and landing pages
- Agency portfolios and creative showcases
- High-end consumer products
- Any project requiring Awwwards-tier quality

